License: CC0-1.0
 The AppStream metadata carries <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>,
 which describes the metadata file itself rather than veetee. Freedesktop
 recommends a permissive licence for metainfo so that distributions and app
 stores can reuse it freely.

Files: crates/vt-fonts/fonts/*
Copyright: 2026 Iain Smith and the veetee contributors
License: OFL-1.1
 The fonts are original pixel designs drawn on DEC's character cell
 geometry. They are not ROM dumps and contain no Digital Equipment
 Corporation code or data.

Files: vendor/*
Copyright: the respective authors of each crate
License: permissive
 The vendor directory holds the crates.io dependencies named in Cargo.lock,
 vendored so that the package builds without network access. Every one is
 under a permissive licence -- MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode or
 similar -- which is enforced upstream by cargo-deny; no copyleft crate is
 permitted. Each crate keeps its own licence files inside its directory, and
 THIRD-PARTY.md in the source root lists them with their licences.

